"Husk needs memory it can write and then execute, which on iOS takes an attached debugger. There are two ways to get it: a debugger that services trap requests, or a MAP_JIT mapping, which the kernel allows any debugged process. Either one is enough — which is available depends on the device and the iOS version, so Husk tests both rather than assuming." = "Husk 需要可寫入後再執行的記憶體，在 iOS 上這需要連接著的偵錯程式。取得方式有兩種：處理陷阱請求的偵錯程式，或 MAP_JIT 對映——核心允許任何受偵錯的程序使用 MAP_JIT。任一種都足夠——哪一種可用取決於裝置和 iOS 版本，所以 Husk 會兩種都測試，而不是預先假設。";
"Husk pretends to be a computer on your Wi-Fi, and your %@ pairs with it the way it would with a Mac." = "Husk 會在你的 Wi-Fi 上假裝成一臺電腦，你的 %@ 會像與 Mac 配對一樣與它配對。";
"Husk restores a saved machine instead of booting it, which takes seconds rather than minutes. The picture freezes while it writes. With this off, nothing saves by itself — including after an install." = "Husk 會還原已儲存的機器而不是重新開機，只需幾秒而不是幾分鐘。寫入時畫面會凍結。關閉此選項後，任何東西都不會自動儲存——包括安裝之後。";
"Husk runs a real Android system and opens APKs inside it. A few questions first — all of them can be changed later in Settings." = "Husk 執行真正的 Android 系統，並在其中開啟 APK。先回答幾個問題——全都可以之後在「設定」中更改。";
"Husk runs unmodified Android APKs in a real Android system on your iPhone. The console shows Husk's live log, the guest's serial output and QEMU's own output — the three files any problem here is diagnosed from." = "Husk 在你 iPhone 上的真正 Android 系統中執行未經修改的 Android APK。主控台顯示 Husk 的即時日誌、客體的序列輸出和 QEMU 自己的輸出——這是診斷這裡任何問題所依據的三份檔案。";
"Husk was marked as debugged when it opened, so JIT is on." = "Husk 開啟時已被標記為除錯中，因此 JIT 已開啟。";
"Husk's helper reaches this %@'s debugging service through a local VPN. Nothing leaves your %@." = "Husk 的輔助工具透過本地 VPN 連到這臺 %@ 的偵錯服務。沒有任何資料會離開你的 %@。";
"If JIT is not on when Android starts, Husk turns it on with the method you chose, or walks you through setting one up. You can change it any time in Settings › JIT & sideload." = "如果 Android 啟動時 JIT 尚未開啟，Husk 會用你選擇的方法開啟它，或引導你設定一個。你隨時可以在「設定」›「JIT 與側載」中更改。";
